WEBVTT

00:00:01.575 --> 00:00:02.866
[PHOENIX] Maya signed up for
advanced spiritual training

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:05.491
at Hazakura Temple up in
the snow-capped mountains,

00:00:05.575 --> 00:00:07.366
and Pearl and I tagged along.

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:09.908
There I met someone who
was strangely familiar.

00:00:09.991 --> 00:00:12.408
Her name was Iris and she
was the spitting image

00:00:12.491 --> 00:00:14.908
of Dahlia Hawthorne,
my old flame.

00:00:14.991 --> 00:00:16.575
Later that night,
after Maya crossed

00:00:16.658 --> 00:00:19.575
the infamous Dusky Bridge
to begin her training,

00:00:19.658 --> 00:00:21.408
all hell broke loose.

00:00:21.491 --> 00:00:23.616
Acclaimed children's book
author and illustrator,

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:27.241
Elise Deauxnim, was murdered on
the grounds of the main temple.

00:00:27.325 --> 00:00:28.491
Adding to the chaos,

00:00:28.575 --> 00:00:30.741
a lightning strike
incinerated Dusky Bridge,

00:00:30.825 --> 00:00:34.450
leaving Maya completely stranded
on the other side of the ravine.

00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:36.325
I tried to save her.

00:00:36.408 --> 00:00:38.075
[BUTZ]
Nicky!

00:00:38.158 --> 00:00:39.741
[PHOENIX screams]

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:43.283
[PHOENIX] When law
enforcement finally arrived,

00:00:43.366 --> 00:00:46.658
they arrested Iris
for Elise's murder.

00:00:46.741 --> 00:00:48.325
I believe in her innocence,

00:00:48.408 --> 00:00:50.991
so I entrusted my old
friend Miles with the case

00:00:51.075 --> 00:00:53.700
and my defense attorney's badge.

00:02:32.825 --> 00:02:33.908
[MILES]
Although I can't say I'm

00:02:33.991 --> 00:02:36.158
enjoying these
frigid temperatures,

00:02:36.241 --> 00:02:40.116
it is interesting to visit
the site of Dusky Bridge.

00:02:41.283 --> 00:02:44.616
[GUMSHOE]
Whoa, Prosecutor Edgeworth!

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.825
[MILES]
Hello, Gumshoe.

00:02:46.908 --> 00:02:48.491
It's been too long, sir!

00:02:48.575 --> 00:02:51.200
I heard you'd be here, so I
busted out the ol' kneepads

00:02:51.283 --> 00:02:52.491
to work this case!

00:02:52.575 --> 00:02:54.408
[MILES] Honestly,
I'd expect no less from you.

00:02:54.491 --> 00:02:56.783
[GUMSHOE] So rest assured
you'll have "Big" Dick Gumshoe

00:02:56.866 --> 00:02:58.700
at your service
whenever you need me!

00:02:58.783 --> 00:03:01.658
That so? Appreciate it.

00:03:01.741 --> 00:03:02.991
Full disclosure,

00:03:03.075 --> 00:03:05.908
there's something that
I need to tell you first.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:10.158
[GUMSHOE]
Objection!

00:03:10.241 --> 00:03:11.491
You gotta be kidding me, pal!

00:03:11.575 --> 00:03:14.450
You're really gonna
defend Sister Iris?!

00:03:14.533 --> 00:03:16.908
Yes. It was a shock
to me as well.

00:03:16.991 --> 00:03:18.491
[GUMSHOE]
But how can you be a prosecutor

00:03:18.575 --> 00:03:20.033
that's not a prosecutor?!

00:03:20.116 --> 00:03:22.158
"Prosecutor Edgeworth
standing for the Defense"

00:03:22.241 --> 00:03:23.283
makes my brain hurt!

00:03:23.366 --> 00:03:25.741
It's like a crime
against nature!

00:03:25.825 --> 00:03:27.908
Regardless, I'll need
a briefing from you.

00:03:27.991 --> 00:03:29.366
Uh--

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:31.616
But a cop giving the defense
that kind of inside scoop

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:35.241
could get into some murky
territory, ethically speaking.

00:03:35.325 --> 00:03:36.950
[MILES]
Don't let that get in your way.

00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:40.158
All you have to do is leak it to
me without telling anyone else.

00:03:40.241 --> 00:03:42.241
[GUMSHOE]
Hmm...

00:03:42.325 --> 00:03:44.825
I'll be leakier than
a discount diaper!

00:03:44.908 --> 00:03:47.575
Just... be discrete.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.866
So, as I understand it,

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:55.825
Maya Fey is stuck in a temple
on the other side of this gorge.

00:03:55.908 --> 00:03:57.866
[GUMSHOE] Yeah, and with all
this wind whippin' around,

00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:59.950
an aerial extraction's
off the table.

00:04:00.033 --> 00:04:02.116
She's there till tomorrow
at the very least.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.491
In this bitter cold.

00:04:03.575 --> 00:04:05.366
I hope she's okay.

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:06.616
I'm curious.

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:09.033
Do you know what caused
the bridge to burn?

00:04:09.116 --> 00:04:10.575
[GUMSHOE]
It was a lightning bolt.

00:04:10.658 --> 00:04:13.991
After it quit snowing, there was
some kinda electrical storm.

00:04:14.075 --> 00:04:15.533
Completely fried the bridge.

00:04:15.616 --> 00:04:17.658
[MILES] Looks like there's
another building that way.

00:04:17.741 --> 00:04:18.908
[GUMSHOE]
All right, pal.

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:20.450
We should head over
to the main temple

00:04:20.533 --> 00:04:22.575
and see what the
eyewitness has to say.

00:04:22.658 --> 00:04:23.741
[MILES gasps]

00:04:23.825 --> 00:04:26.533
An eyewitness? Really?

00:04:26.616 --> 00:04:30.283
Yep! The Bikini lady saw it all.

00:04:30.366 --> 00:04:32.908
[MILES]
O...kay...

00:04:35.491 --> 00:04:38.575
[MILES] Well, I don't
see a bikini anywhere.

00:04:38.658 --> 00:04:40.450
I know I'm probably
not what you expected,

00:04:40.533 --> 00:04:43.033
but I gotta bundle it up
for the cold weather.

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:45.158
Come back this summer.

00:04:45.241 --> 00:04:47.950
I shoulda made it clear we'd
be talkin' to Sister Bikini,

00:04:48.033 --> 00:04:50.325
the head nun, but I totally
thought the same thing.

00:04:50.408 --> 00:04:52.950
Details like that are
important, Detective.

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:54.825
And perhaps you should
take this as a clue

00:04:54.908 --> 00:04:56.741
to why you have
never gotten a raise.

00:04:56.825 --> 00:04:58.408
You're right about that, sir.

00:04:58.491 --> 00:04:59.825
Sister.

00:04:59.908 --> 00:05:01.783
Can you tell me what
happened last night?

00:05:01.866 --> 00:05:03.783
I took the trainee over
to the Inner Temple,

00:05:03.866 --> 00:05:06.325
where she'd be doing
her spiritual exercises.

00:05:06.408 --> 00:05:08.700
By "trainee" you mean Maya Fey?

00:05:08.783 --> 00:05:09.783
[BIKINI]
Yep.

00:05:09.866 --> 00:05:11.366
The training lasts
all night long

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:12.825
and the head nun has to be there

00:05:12.908 --> 00:05:14.783
to observe throughout
the process.

00:05:14.866 --> 00:05:16.408
[MILES]
So you're there all night.

00:05:16.491 --> 00:05:19.450
But didn't the incident occur
over here in the courtyard?

00:05:19.533 --> 00:05:21.033
[sighs]

00:05:21.116 --> 00:05:23.450
I did have to leave
my post for a bit,

00:05:23.533 --> 00:05:25.366
but Iris took over for me.

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:26.991
So Iris was there?

00:05:27.075 --> 00:05:29.283
[BIKINI] My lower back's
been giving me trouble.

00:05:29.366 --> 00:05:31.241
Iris came to see
how I was holding up

00:05:31.325 --> 00:05:33.325
and told me she'd sub in for me

00:05:33.408 --> 00:05:36.783
so I could get some
decent rest in my own room.

00:05:36.866 --> 00:05:39.616
And then at 10 PM I rang
the bell for lights out.

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:43.033
After that, I was in my room
until I heard all the commotion.

00:05:43.116 --> 00:05:44.575
I headed back to
the Inner Temple

00:05:44.658 --> 00:05:46.533
to check on things after a bit

00:05:46.616 --> 00:05:48.575
and that's when I saw
it in the courtyard!

00:05:48.658 --> 00:05:50.075
What did you see?

00:05:50.158 --> 00:05:52.450
It was like it was something
straight out of a nightmare!

00:05:52.533 --> 00:05:53.283
[BIKINI whimpers]

00:05:53.366 --> 00:05:55.116
No... I can't...

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.616
I can't even say it!

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:57.450
What?

00:05:57.533 --> 00:05:59.075
[BIKINI wails]

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:00.783
[BIKINI]
Iris... She...

00:06:00.866 --> 00:06:02.908
Are you saying Iris
was in the courtyard?

00:06:02.991 --> 00:06:05.241
I saw her with my own eyes!

00:06:05.325 --> 00:06:09.616
How could that gentle girl
do something so horrific?!

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:12.533
I screamed bloody murder
and then passed out.

00:06:12.616 --> 00:06:17.033
I only came to when that spiky-
haired man ran across my belly.

00:06:17.116 --> 00:06:19.283
[MILES] That corroborates
Wright's story.

00:06:19.366 --> 00:06:21.325
And she doesn't
appear to be lying.

00:06:21.408 --> 00:06:23.533
[BIKINI cries, blows nose]

00:06:23.616 --> 00:06:26.116
[GUMSHOE]
Ew, that's disgusting!

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.116
Is there anything else
you'd like to mention?

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:30.450
Yes, come to think of
it, there is something.

00:06:30.533 --> 00:06:33.241
I have no idea where
Pearl ran off to!

00:06:33.325 --> 00:06:34.825
Who might that be?

00:06:34.908 --> 00:06:38.283
A sweetheart of a little girl
who came here with the trainee.

00:06:38.366 --> 00:06:39.991
I haven't seen her all day,

00:06:40.075 --> 00:06:42.741
but I heard she went up to
Elise's room last night.

00:06:42.825 --> 00:06:44.241
You mean the victim?

00:06:44.325 --> 00:06:47.325
[sobs] It's all because...

00:06:47.408 --> 00:06:50.658
This happened because
of my creaky old back!

00:06:50.741 --> 00:06:53.658
[BIKINI wailing]

00:06:56.783 --> 00:07:00.033
I got a search together
for little Pearl Fey.

00:07:00.116 --> 00:07:01.366
Good work.

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:02.866
So the crime scene--

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:04.200
We took the body, of course,

00:07:04.283 --> 00:07:06.616
but everything else is
practically untouched.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:07.991
[MILES]
That's the murder weapon?

00:07:08.075 --> 00:07:11.866
[GUMSHOE] Seven-pointed sword,
the "Shi-something."

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:13.700
[MILES]
Any info on the victim?

00:07:13.783 --> 00:07:15.033
Yessir.

00:07:15.116 --> 00:07:16.825
All we know is that she
was a picture book author

00:07:16.908 --> 00:07:18.533
who went by Elise Deauxnim.

00:07:18.616 --> 00:07:20.408
Don't know her real
name or much else

00:07:20.491 --> 00:07:22.450
besides she won
an award last year.

00:07:22.533 --> 00:07:24.491
That kind of privacy
is rare these days.

00:07:24.575 --> 00:07:25.908
[GUMSHOE]
Time of death is estimated

00:07:25.991 --> 00:07:28.575
between 10 and 11 PM last night.

00:07:28.658 --> 00:07:30.408
The cause is being
ruled as blood loss

00:07:30.491 --> 00:07:32.450
resulting from a
stab to the back.

00:07:32.533 --> 00:07:33.700
That poor woman.

00:07:33.783 --> 00:07:35.700
And you should probably
know the victim's body

00:07:35.783 --> 00:07:38.116
was practically covered
head to toe with bruises!

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:38.950
[MILES]
Really?

00:07:39.033 --> 00:07:39.908
Yeah.

00:07:39.991 --> 00:07:41.116
They seem to be consistent

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:44.075
with falling out of a
second-story window.

00:07:44.158 --> 00:07:46.866
[MILES] Like the one in
the room above us, correct?

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:49.158
Which just so happens
to be the exact room

00:07:49.241 --> 00:07:51.325
the victim was
staying in last night!

00:07:51.408 --> 00:07:52.825
[MILES]
Interesting.

00:07:52.908 --> 00:07:54.908
Leads me to believe she may
have been pushed from there

00:07:54.991 --> 00:07:57.075
and then stabbed with the sword.

00:07:57.158 --> 00:07:58.325
What's that?

00:07:58.408 --> 00:07:59.741
The victim's fingerprints
were all over it,

00:07:59.825 --> 00:08:02.075
so we're guessing it's
some kind of cane she used.

00:08:02.158 --> 00:08:04.075
Oh, speaking of fingerprints.

00:08:04.158 --> 00:08:05.658
Yes, what?

00:08:05.741 --> 00:08:08.116
[GUMSHOE] That crazy sword,
the murder weapon,

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:11.408
had the accused's
fingerprints on it, too.

00:08:11.491 --> 00:08:14.408
That sort of evidence
will be difficult to refute.

00:08:14.491 --> 00:08:16.033
Whoops, it totally
slipped my mind

00:08:16.116 --> 00:08:18.658
that you're the
defense, Prosecutor.

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:24.575
[MILES] Things definitely
seem desperate right now.

00:08:24.658 --> 00:08:27.033
Is this how Wright felt
every time he stood in court

00:08:27.116 --> 00:08:29.491
for one of his clients?

00:08:29.575 --> 00:08:31.033
You weren't kidding
when you said

00:08:31.116 --> 00:08:32.783
you're gonna be the
defense attorney, were ya?

00:08:32.866 --> 00:08:33.908
No.

00:08:33.991 --> 00:08:35.366
But you're a pretty
famous prosecutor,

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:36.825
so won't that be a problem

00:08:36.908 --> 00:08:38.950
when they see you walking
into the courtroom tomorrow?

00:08:39.033 --> 00:08:40.200
[MILES]
I realize that,

00:08:40.283 --> 00:08:42.325
which is precisely the
reason why I arranged

00:08:42.408 --> 00:08:44.741
to have a different judge
presiding over this case.

00:08:44.825 --> 00:08:46.408
[GUMSHOE]
Okay, well, we've been waiting

00:08:46.491 --> 00:08:47.783
for Godot to get back to us,

00:08:47.866 --> 00:08:49.950
'cause he's supposed
to be the prosecutor.

00:08:50.033 --> 00:08:51.283
Not a problem.

00:08:51.366 --> 00:08:53.658
I've made arrangements
for a prosecutor as well.

00:08:53.741 --> 00:08:55.283
[GUMSHOE stammers]

00:08:55.366 --> 00:08:56.783
[MILES]
Problem?

00:08:56.866 --> 00:08:58.366
Nope, that's just the sound
of my mind being blown away

00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:00.283
by how amazing you are!

00:09:00.366 --> 00:09:01.741
[sighs]

00:09:01.825 --> 00:09:03.366
Let's go.

00:09:08.658 --> 00:09:10.116
[GUMSHOE]
Crazy, I didn't even know

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:12.200
there was a shack over here.

00:09:14.825 --> 00:09:17.075
[BUTZ]
I knew you'd come.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.200
Edgy boy.

00:09:20.283 --> 00:09:21.408
Hello, Larry.

00:09:21.491 --> 00:09:23.491
You took your time.
What've you been doing?

00:09:23.575 --> 00:09:25.033
[MILES] I should be
asking you that question.

00:09:25.116 --> 00:09:25.908
Huh?

00:09:25.991 --> 00:09:27.366
I'm saying I don't understand

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:29.408
why you're even here
in the first place.

00:09:29.491 --> 00:09:30.950
Come on, bro!

00:09:31.033 --> 00:09:33.700
I'm an artist, so I'm working on
some snowy landscape pieces.

00:09:33.783 --> 00:09:36.366
An artist? Surely you jest.

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:39.450
This guy was apparently the dead
picture book lady's apprentice.

00:09:39.533 --> 00:09:41.533
That so? This dullard?

00:09:41.616 --> 00:09:43.700
Hey man, why you
gotta call me that?

00:09:43.783 --> 00:09:46.283
I'm Laurice Deauxnim,
the artiste,

00:09:46.366 --> 00:09:49.283
and I'm here to do a
study of Dusky Bridge!

00:09:54.158 --> 00:09:55.325
[BUTZ]
What's up with Iris?

00:09:55.408 --> 00:09:57.741
Have the po-po finally
let her outta jail yet?

00:09:57.825 --> 00:09:59.700
She will be standing
trial tomorrow.

00:09:59.783 --> 00:10:01.283
It's not lookin' good, pal.

00:10:01.366 --> 00:10:03.491
[BUTZ] That's the craziest
thing I've ever heard!

00:10:03.575 --> 00:10:06.075
There's no way in hell
she could be the killer!

00:10:06.158 --> 00:10:08.825
And what makes you so
certain of her innocence?

00:10:08.908 --> 00:10:10.658
I mean, you guys have
seen her, haven't you?

00:10:10.741 --> 00:10:13.741
She's way too cute
to be a murderer.

00:10:13.825 --> 00:10:16.033
[MILES]
Why did I even ask?

00:10:16.116 --> 00:10:17.616
[BUTZ]
But man, in my opinion,

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:19.616
a beautiful girl like
her shouldn't be taking

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:21.450
those kinds of risks.

00:10:21.533 --> 00:10:22.783
[MILES]
What's that mean?

00:10:22.866 --> 00:10:25.241
[BUTZ] Nothing! Just one
of those Butz brain farts!

00:10:25.325 --> 00:10:26.700
As I understand it,

00:10:26.783 --> 00:10:28.533
you're actually the one who
called the cops last night

00:10:28.616 --> 00:10:30.283
after the body was
found, aren't ya?

00:10:30.366 --> 00:10:31.450
Is that true?

00:10:31.533 --> 00:10:33.533
Huh? Oh, yeah, right.

00:10:33.616 --> 00:10:35.283
Man, that was insanity!

00:10:35.366 --> 00:10:38.783
First, the lightning was all
like "crashentino," "zaparroo,"

00:10:38.866 --> 00:10:41.741
there goes the bridge and
Nick whizzing right off it!

00:10:41.825 --> 00:10:44.200
[MILES] I don't speak your
made-up language, Larry.

00:10:44.283 --> 00:10:46.158
Anyway, Nick had run
up screaming at me

00:10:46.241 --> 00:10:49.325
to call the cops, so I did,
and boy howdy was I a mess.

00:10:49.408 --> 00:10:50.616
With the lightning, the fire,

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:52.575
and your buddy whizzing
off the bridge,

00:10:52.658 --> 00:10:54.325
I mean, how could
anybody not be?

00:10:54.408 --> 00:10:56.991
Oh, naw, it's because of the
totally bonkers thing I'd seen

00:10:57.075 --> 00:10:58.116
before all that happened!

00:10:58.200 --> 00:10:59.366
Uh--

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:01.825
You care to elaborate on that?

00:11:01.908 --> 00:11:03.533
Well--I told you
everything I know

00:11:03.616 --> 00:11:05.033
so you should be on your way.

00:11:05.116 --> 00:11:08.616
Larry, you're hiding
something from me, aren't you?

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:10.408
I'm offended that one
of my oldest friends

00:11:10.491 --> 00:11:12.366
can't tell when I'm telling
the honest-to-god truth.

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:14.825
I can tell, that's how
I know you're lying now.

00:11:14.908 --> 00:11:16.533
You better start
talking, pronto,

00:11:16.616 --> 00:11:18.658
or we're gonna throw
your butt in the slammer!

00:11:18.741 --> 00:11:20.158
[screams]

00:11:20.241 --> 00:11:21.533
Quit hassling me, bro!

00:11:21.616 --> 00:11:22.533
[GUMSHOE]
Hey!

00:11:22.616 --> 00:11:25.158
Don't make me have to chase you!

00:11:26.825 --> 00:11:28.116
[MILES]
Your choice.

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:29.825
But I will drag you
into the courtroom

00:11:29.908 --> 00:11:32.783
if that's what it takes
to hear the whole story,

00:11:32.866 --> 00:11:34.450
old friend.

00:11:41.366 --> 00:11:43.700
[JUDGE 204A] And now, this
court is hereby in session

00:11:43.783 --> 00:11:45.783
for the trial of Sister Iris.

00:11:45.866 --> 00:11:49.116
The defense is ready to present
our argument, Your Honor.

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:52.241
[MILES] It is a prosecutor's
duty to doubt the defendant,

00:11:52.325 --> 00:11:54.825
but today I must take
an opposite approach.

00:11:54.908 --> 00:11:56.408
Wright told me
a defense attorney

00:11:56.491 --> 00:11:58.241
must believe in their
client's innocence

00:11:58.325 --> 00:12:00.908
through to the last
moments of the trial.

00:12:00.991 --> 00:12:03.866
Am I truly up to the task?

00:12:06.908 --> 00:12:09.533
I am fully prepared
to defend my client!

00:12:09.616 --> 00:12:11.033
[JUDGE 204A]
Mm.

00:12:11.116 --> 00:12:12.450
If the prosecution is ready,

00:12:12.533 --> 00:12:15.408
then we shall begin without
further ad--[groans]

00:12:15.491 --> 00:12:17.700
Does my whip feel ready to you?

00:12:17.783 --> 00:12:19.700
[JUDGE 204A]
Oh, and you are?

00:12:20.825 --> 00:12:22.283
[FRANZISKA]
My name?

00:12:22.366 --> 00:12:24.366
Franziska von Karma.

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:27.950
Uh, really? Like the
legendary prosecutor?

00:12:28.033 --> 00:12:29.908
That von Karma?

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:33.991
[FRANZISKA]
"Legendary" describes the past,

00:12:34.075 --> 00:12:36.491
but I am bringing
us into the future!

00:12:36.575 --> 00:12:38.491
[JUDGE 204A gasps]

00:12:40.116 --> 00:12:41.283
[MILES]
She left home for America

00:12:41.366 --> 00:12:43.241
and became a prosecutor at 13.

00:12:43.325 --> 00:12:46.658
And like her father, she'll
do whatever it takes to win.

00:12:46.741 --> 00:12:49.366
I'm glad you're here, Franziska.

00:12:51.825 --> 00:12:53.075
[JUDGE 204A clears throat]

00:12:53.158 --> 00:12:54.533
Guess that's been cleared up.

00:12:54.616 --> 00:12:56.908
But I do have a question
for the defense.

00:12:56.991 --> 00:12:58.116
[MILES]
Yes, Your Honor?

00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:00.200
I can't help feeling
I've met a prosecutor

00:13:00.283 --> 00:13:02.200
to whom you bear such
an uncanny resemblance.

00:13:02.283 --> 00:13:04.575
He could practically
be your twin brother.

00:13:04.658 --> 00:13:06.450
Must've imagined it.

00:13:06.533 --> 00:13:09.575
Prosecutor von Karma, do you
know who I'm talking about?

00:13:09.658 --> 00:13:11.325
[FRANZISKA]
You imagined it.

00:13:11.408 --> 00:13:13.241
Why would I invent
such a person?

00:13:13.325 --> 00:13:15.866
[FRANZISKA] I had expected
that I would be squaring off

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:18.408
against Phoenix Wright
in the courtroom today.

00:13:18.491 --> 00:13:21.158
But perhaps this is the battle
I've been preparing for

00:13:21.241 --> 00:13:23.366
my entire life.

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:28.450
This is my chance to crush Miles
Edgeworth once and for all!

00:13:29.908 --> 00:13:31.491
Prosecution, with
that out of the way,

00:13:31.575 --> 00:13:33.950
please begin your
opening statement.

00:13:34.033 --> 00:13:35.866
[FRANZISKA] The victim
is children's book author

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:37.866
and illustrator, Elise Deauxnim.

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:39.325
Her bloody corpse was discovered

00:13:39.408 --> 00:13:41.616
in the courtyard of
Hazakura Temple.

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:44.116
As seen here, she was
stabbed through the torso

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:47.408
with a ceremonial sword
held by a golden statue.

00:13:47.491 --> 00:13:49.408
What an awful tragedy.

00:13:49.491 --> 00:13:53.033
An act of brutality clearly
carried out by Sister Iris.

00:13:53.116 --> 00:13:55.825
The proof? Well, it was all seen

00:13:55.908 --> 00:13:58.783
by an eyewitness with
an honest reputation.

00:13:58.866 --> 00:14:00.366
Let's hear them out.

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:04.783
Very well. Please bring the
witness to the stand at once.

00:14:04.866 --> 00:14:06.408
[MILES]
And so it begins--

00:14:06.491 --> 00:14:11.158
my first and my last trial
as a defense attorney.

00:14:11.241 --> 00:14:14.866
[FRANZISKA] Witness,
state your name and occupation.

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:16.491
Your Honor, I'm the
head nun in charge

00:14:16.575 --> 00:14:17.991
over at the Hazakura Temple,

00:14:18.075 --> 00:14:20.866
and my name is Bikini, but
don't get the wrong idea okay?

00:14:20.950 --> 00:14:23.825
It does cause one to conjure
up certain ima--[groans]

00:14:23.908 --> 00:14:25.825
[FRANZISKA] This courtroom
is a sacred place.

00:14:25.908 --> 00:14:27.575
Those who enter it
with impure thoughts

00:14:27.658 --> 00:14:29.616
should be forced to leave
without exception!

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:31.783
You think I should
leave my own courtroom?

00:14:31.866 --> 00:14:34.366
Now there's no need to go
gettin' your bikini in a twist

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:37.241
until you see me in my
preferred summer attire.

00:14:37.325 --> 00:14:38.241
[laughs]

00:14:38.325 --> 00:14:39.658
So about the murder.

00:14:39.741 --> 00:14:41.741
You claim to have seen
the crime take place,

00:14:41.825 --> 00:14:43.616
is that correct, Sister?

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:45.533
I'm afraid I did.

00:14:45.616 --> 00:14:48.241
I'm shocked my sweet
little Iris could do this.

00:14:48.325 --> 00:14:50.200
[JUDGE 204A]
This may be difficult for you,

00:14:50.283 --> 00:14:52.075
but please describe
the events of that night

00:14:52.158 --> 00:14:53.866
as accurately as possible.

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:55.366
[BIKINI]
Mm-hmm.

00:14:57.991 --> 00:15:00.158
On that night,
I was helping a trainee

00:15:00.241 --> 00:15:02.658
begin her exercises
in the Inner Temple.

00:15:02.741 --> 00:15:05.366
Then around 10 PM,
Iris came for me.

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:06.741
She stayed to help the trainee

00:15:06.825 --> 00:15:08.575
and I went back to
the main grounds.

00:15:08.658 --> 00:15:09.908
[MILES]
Hold it!

00:15:09.991 --> 00:15:11.283
That can't be true,

00:15:11.366 --> 00:15:13.241
because the defendant never
went to the Inner Temple

00:15:13.325 --> 00:15:15.241
on the night in question.

00:15:15.325 --> 00:15:17.908
Isn't that correct, defendant?

00:15:17.991 --> 00:15:20.200
I was in my room in
Hazakura Temple all night

00:15:20.283 --> 00:15:23.075
up until I heard the commotion
outside when the body was found.

00:15:23.158 --> 00:15:25.200
I swear I saw her
with my own eyes!

00:15:25.283 --> 00:15:27.908
She was dressed exactly the
same as at dinner earlier!

00:15:27.991 --> 00:15:29.200
[MILES]
And how was she dressed?

00:15:29.283 --> 00:15:30.700
[BIKINI]
Same robes she always wears

00:15:30.783 --> 00:15:33.408
and with her head scarf
on just like before!

00:15:33.491 --> 00:15:35.741
Unfortunately,
that is also untrue.

00:15:35.825 --> 00:15:37.241
[BIKINI gasps]

00:15:37.325 --> 00:15:39.825
[MILES]
Iris. This head scarf, or hood--

00:15:39.908 --> 00:15:41.325
Had you done anything with it?

00:15:41.408 --> 00:15:42.991
I gave it to Mister Wright

00:15:43.075 --> 00:15:46.241
on my way to ring the bell
for lights out before 10 PM.

00:15:46.325 --> 00:15:47.825
You gave it away?

00:15:47.908 --> 00:15:50.825
[MILES] Indeed. Which means she
wasn't wearing her head scarf

00:15:50.908 --> 00:15:52.408
when the witness claims
to have seen her--

00:15:52.491 --> 00:15:55.116
a fact that begs the question
"who did she see that night"?

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:58.658
Ha! Are you suggesting the
defendant had a doppelganger

00:15:58.741 --> 00:16:00.075
come to the Inner Temple?

00:16:00.158 --> 00:16:02.241
We don't really
know who was there.

00:16:02.325 --> 00:16:05.158
However, this witness
needs to be precise

00:16:05.241 --> 00:16:07.658
with the details
of her testimony.

00:16:07.741 --> 00:16:09.075
[BIKINI]
It's so bizarre!

00:16:09.158 --> 00:16:12.575
I know exactly what
I saw that night.

00:16:12.658 --> 00:16:14.866
[MILES] I don't think
she's purposefully lying.

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:17.783
This contradiction is sure
to come up later in the trial.

00:16:17.866 --> 00:16:20.075
[JUDGE 204A] You may continue
with your testimony, witness,

00:16:20.158 --> 00:16:22.700
but keep in mind you'll need
to be precise in your account.

00:16:22.783 --> 00:16:24.116
Yes.

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:25.783
After resting for a short while,

00:16:25.866 --> 00:16:28.783
I headed back to the
Inner Temple around 11 PM.

00:16:28.866 --> 00:16:31.908
Then, I heard a strange noise
coming from the courtyard.

00:16:31.991 --> 00:16:34.825
When I looked that way,
I saw Iris holding a sword.

00:16:34.908 --> 00:16:38.491
It was plunged to the hilt
into poor Ms. Deauxnim's back!

00:16:38.575 --> 00:16:40.658
I imagine that was a
very traumatizing thing

00:16:40.741 --> 00:16:41.741
for you to witness.

00:16:41.825 --> 00:16:43.325
That's all I remember.

00:16:43.408 --> 00:16:45.075
I let loose a scream
and passed out.

00:16:45.158 --> 00:16:48.241
Are you absolutely certain
that you saw the defendant?

00:16:48.325 --> 00:16:50.116
[BIKINI]
Yes. Without a doubt.

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:52.325
She wasn't wearing her
head scarf at the time,

00:16:52.408 --> 00:16:53.866
but I know it was Iris!

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:56.241
When I awoke,
Ms. Deauxnim was lying dead

00:16:56.325 --> 00:16:59.033
underneath Mystic Ami's
golden statue.

00:16:59.116 --> 00:17:01.283
Game over, Edgeworth.

00:17:01.366 --> 00:17:02.658
You've nowhere to turn.

00:17:02.741 --> 00:17:03.908
[grunts]

00:17:03.991 --> 00:17:05.866
The witness stands by
her damning testimony,

00:17:05.950 --> 00:17:08.491
which is corroborated by the
defendant's fingerprints found

00:17:08.575 --> 00:17:11.116
on the seven-pointed sword that
was used as the murder weapon.

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:13.450
Sister Iris' prints were on it?

00:17:13.533 --> 00:17:16.158
This proves she
murdered Ms. Deauxnim.

00:17:16.241 --> 00:17:19.366
Therefore, this court
must find her guilty.

00:17:22.866 --> 00:17:26.241
[JUDGE 204A] Do you care to make
a counter-argument, defense?

00:17:26.325 --> 00:17:28.908
[MILES] So this is what it's
like to be on the other side.

00:17:28.991 --> 00:17:30.450
Not bad.

00:17:30.533 --> 00:17:32.241
Very well.

00:17:32.325 --> 00:17:36.116
I shall have to find my own
way to turn things around.

00:17:37.325 --> 00:17:38.866
Objection!

00:17:39.908 --> 00:17:42.241
[FRANZISKA gasps, screams]

00:17:42.325 --> 00:17:44.158
[MILES]
Plunged in to the hilt?

00:17:44.241 --> 00:17:47.116
Then the entire blade should
be covered with blood.

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:49.825
But if we check the
crime scene photo...

00:17:50.866 --> 00:17:52.533
[JUDGE 204A]
It's only on the very tip of it!

00:17:52.616 --> 00:17:53.616
[FRANZISKA gasps]

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:55.200
[MILES]
Considering its unique design,

00:17:55.283 --> 00:17:58.033
is it even possible to stab a
person all the way to the hilt

00:17:58.116 --> 00:18:00.283
with this particular sword?

00:18:00.366 --> 00:18:01.575
Th-That's what she saw!

00:18:01.658 --> 00:18:02.908
When I looked over,

00:18:02.991 --> 00:18:04.450
the sword was totally run
through the poor woman

00:18:04.533 --> 00:18:06.866
and the hilt was the
only part sticking out!

00:18:06.950 --> 00:18:08.283
If you'd be clear, defense,

00:18:08.366 --> 00:18:10.283
what is the point you're
trying to make here?

00:18:10.366 --> 00:18:11.741
My point is simple.

00:18:11.825 --> 00:18:14.325
This sword was almost
certainly not the weapon

00:18:14.408 --> 00:18:15.408
used in this murder.

00:18:15.491 --> 00:18:16.991
Don't be foolish.

00:18:17.075 --> 00:18:20.450
[MILES] And if it was indeed not
the weapon used in this crime,

00:18:20.533 --> 00:18:23.325
her fingerprints on it would
have no bearing whatsoever.

00:18:23.408 --> 00:18:26.491
It doesn't prove she
committed the murder!

00:18:26.575 --> 00:18:28.866
[FRANZISKA gasps, groans]

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:31.991
[MILES] Seems to me the
prosecution's chilling claims

00:18:32.075 --> 00:18:34.033
have melted like snow in spring.

00:18:34.116 --> 00:18:35.408
[CROWD murmuring]

00:18:35.491 --> 00:18:36.950
Expertly done.

00:18:37.033 --> 00:18:38.825
You found a major contradiction

00:18:38.908 --> 00:18:41.116
by merely looking at
one piece of evidence.

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:42.950
Who would've imagined
that bloody blade

00:18:43.033 --> 00:18:44.366
wasn't the murder weapon?

00:18:44.450 --> 00:18:45.866
[FRANZISKA]
Objection!

00:18:45.950 --> 00:18:47.408
If that is the case,

00:18:47.491 --> 00:18:49.700
then why don't you take a stab
at answering this question,

00:18:49.783 --> 00:18:51.033
Miles Edgeworth.

00:18:51.116 --> 00:18:53.283
What do you believe was
the actual murder weapon?

00:18:53.366 --> 00:18:54.950
I cannot answer that.

00:18:55.033 --> 00:18:56.491
How typical.

00:18:56.575 --> 00:18:59.741
Even so, no matter the weapon,
the conclusion is the same.

00:18:59.825 --> 00:19:01.783
[JUDGE 204A] What exactly
do you mean by that?

00:19:01.866 --> 00:19:05.241
The witness explicitly stated
what she saw that night.

00:19:05.325 --> 00:19:07.908
She was there to observe
the moment when Sister Iris

00:19:07.991 --> 00:19:11.033
brutally stabbed the victim
in the temple courtyard.

00:19:11.116 --> 00:19:12.116
[groans]

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:14.700
[FRANZISKA]
Isn't that right?

00:19:14.783 --> 00:19:17.950
Oh, gimme a break. I never
said anything of the sort.

00:19:18.033 --> 00:19:19.366
U-Uh--

00:19:19.450 --> 00:19:20.908
[BIKINI] The sword was already
sticking out of her back

00:19:20.991 --> 00:19:22.783
when I came across
them that night.

00:19:22.866 --> 00:19:25.408
Seemed to me that Iris
was just holding it.

00:19:25.491 --> 00:19:27.866
Do you mean to tell this court
that you did not, in fact,

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:29.908
witness the defendant
stabbing the victim?

00:19:29.991 --> 00:19:32.533
Yeah, just seeing that
would've killed me, too!

00:19:32.616 --> 00:19:34.533
--[CROWD gasps]
--No way.

00:19:34.616 --> 00:19:36.116
[MILES]
However,

00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:38.158
since it's quite obvious there
was a different murder weapon,

00:19:38.241 --> 00:19:40.158
we must ask what became of that.

00:19:40.241 --> 00:19:41.408
[FRANZISKA]
What do you mean?

00:19:41.491 --> 00:19:42.950
Following the incident,

00:19:43.033 --> 00:19:45.283
the local police conducted a
thorough investigative search

00:19:45.366 --> 00:19:46.616
of the surrounding area.

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:49.283
Yes, they did their
jobs quite well.

00:19:49.366 --> 00:19:52.616
But nothing suspicious was found
on or near the temple grounds.

00:19:52.700 --> 00:19:56.700
I see. That's very
peculiar indeed.

00:19:56.783 --> 00:19:59.700
Although there is an extremely
secure hiding place nearby.

00:19:59.783 --> 00:20:01.241
Is that so?

00:20:01.325 --> 00:20:03.825
If it were disposed of there,
it may never be discovered.

00:20:03.908 --> 00:20:05.158
Where might that be?

00:20:05.241 --> 00:20:06.575
[FRANZISKA]
Eagle River.

00:20:06.658 --> 00:20:08.116
[MILES]
Really?

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:11.200
There was a snowmobile next to
Hazakura Temple's main gate.

00:20:11.283 --> 00:20:13.116
Somebody could have driven
this over to the bridge

00:20:13.200 --> 00:20:15.825
and thrown the weapon into the
gorge where the rapid current

00:20:15.908 --> 00:20:17.866
would whisk it away
to who knows where.

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:20.158
Uh--the snowmobile?

00:20:20.241 --> 00:20:23.116
Have you any proof of
this, or just conjecture?

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:25.450
Do I? Of course I have proof.

00:20:25.533 --> 00:20:26.866
[MILES]
Nonsense!

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:28.450
[FRANZISKA] There were
snowmobile tracks leading from

00:20:28.533 --> 00:20:31.825
Hazakura Temple to Dusky Bridge
that were made that very night.

00:20:31.908 --> 00:20:33.116
[gasps]

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:35.533
It makes sense if you
consider another weapon.

00:20:35.616 --> 00:20:37.908
The killer drove there to
get rid of the evidence.

00:20:37.991 --> 00:20:39.283
Tell us, witness.

00:20:39.366 --> 00:20:41.533
Who could have used the
snowmobile that night?

00:20:41.616 --> 00:20:44.408
Well, just Iris.
She's the only one.

00:20:44.491 --> 00:20:46.658
What? Why just her?

00:20:46.741 --> 00:20:49.408
[BIKINI] Because she had the
only key to the snowmobile.

00:20:49.491 --> 00:20:53.158
Iris! Did you really do this?

00:20:53.241 --> 00:20:55.200
[MILES]
Iris...

00:20:55.283 --> 00:20:59.241
I'm so sorry, Sister...
but I can't answer that.

00:20:59.325 --> 00:21:00.450
Not right now.

00:21:00.533 --> 00:21:01.825
--[CROWD murmuring]
--[JUDGE 204A] Order!

00:21:01.908 --> 00:21:02.991
--[CROWD murmuring]
--I demand order in this court!

00:21:03.075 --> 00:21:04.700
Seems you've failed, Edgeworth.

00:21:04.783 --> 00:21:06.450
So admit defeat.

00:21:06.533 --> 00:21:07.491
[MILES grunts]

00:21:07.575 --> 00:21:09.658
[MILES]
Iris, why won't you answer?

00:21:09.741 --> 00:21:12.033
Your Honor, the defendant's
stubborn refusal

00:21:12.116 --> 00:21:13.700
is practically a confession!

00:21:13.783 --> 00:21:15.825
I demand a verdict this instant!

00:21:15.908 --> 00:21:18.116
If the defendant will
not speak on her behalf,

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:21.033
I see no need to continue
this trial any further.

00:21:21.116 --> 00:21:22.241
[BUTZ grunts]

00:21:23.658 --> 00:21:25.366
[BUTZ]
Objection!

00:21:26.908 --> 00:21:28.950
[JUDGE 204A]
Wait, who in the hell are you?

00:21:29.033 --> 00:21:32.491
Gotta say, this performance
is kinda hard to watch.

00:21:33.533 --> 00:21:35.033
[MILES]
Larry!

00:21:35.116 --> 00:21:38.158
Sorry, Vincent van Bro, but you
can call me Laurice Deauxnim.

00:21:38.241 --> 00:21:39.575
Did he say Deauxnim?

00:21:39.658 --> 00:21:41.741
[BUTZ] Everything that
happened that night--

00:21:41.825 --> 00:21:44.366
I saw it all.

00:21:44.450 --> 00:21:46.741
And if I can save my
beautiful little flower,

00:21:46.825 --> 00:21:49.908
I'll paint you a masterpiece
with my testimony!

00:23:20.575 --> 00:23:21.700
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:23:21.783 --> 00:23:23.575
Larry's sudden appearance
in the courtroom

00:23:23.658 --> 00:23:25.950
may be what turns this
whole case around.

00:23:26.033 --> 00:23:28.575
His artistic rendering provides
a crucial piece of info

00:23:28.658 --> 00:23:29.825
that shocks everyone.

00:23:29.908 --> 00:23:31.950
And as rookie defense
attorney Miles Edgeworth

00:23:32.033 --> 00:23:34.616
defies von Karma's relentless
line of questioning,

00:23:34.700 --> 00:23:36.741
he discovers a
glaring contradiction.

00:23:36.825 --> 00:23:39.283
Also, I make my
triumphant return!

00:23:39.366 --> 00:23:40.783
I'm back in the saddle, Miles,

00:23:40.866 --> 00:23:43.241
and I'll ride the facts
straight into justice!

00:23:43.325 --> 00:23:45.616
Find the contradictions!
Believe in the truth!

00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:48.491
Next episode: "Bridge to
the Turnabout - 3rd Trial"!

00:23:48.575 --> 00:23:49.866
Take that!
